      <h2>Case Study: Gamification Launch</h2>

      <h3>Challenge</h3>
      <p>The ExtraCare team decided to launch a gamification test program to increase shopper engagement, by creating routines in our customers. While acting as the lead product designer for the project (more on that here), I was also tasked with ensuring the creative direction for the entire campaign was unified across every narrative touch point.</p>

      <h3>Strategy</h3>
      <p>I acted as the creative strategist and "central node" for the entire cross-functional launch. I established the unified creative vision and designed the framework that connected disparate teams, including:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>In store assets:</strong> Partnering with the Store Experience team to curate Banners, Aisle Caps, Blades, Stanchions, mats, etc. as part of the awareness entry points of this new campaign.</li>
        <li><strong>Marketing communications:</strong> Partnering with the CRM, marketing ops and campaign teams to ensure consistent language, messaging and imagery throughout engagement campaigns.</li>
        <li><strong>Digital experiences:</strong> Led the design and development of every asset utilized across .com, app, and in-store digital experiences, which would then become the basis for the direction followed by other teams.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>The Value</h3>
      <p>By serving as the creative bridge, I eliminated cross-departmental silos, ensured absolute brand consistency across the entire user journey, and streamlined the production pipeline for an on-time, highly successful launch.</p>

      <!-- In-Store Assets & Entry Points -->
      <div class="image-grid-2">
        <img src="/images/creative-direction/live_06.png" alt="In-store campaign assets 1" loading="lazy" />
        <img src="/images/creative-direction/live_07.png" alt="In-store campaign assets 2" loading="lazy" />
