      <h2>Case Study: Scaling a Brand System</h2>

      <h3>Challenge</h3>
      <p>The existing creative direction for the ExtraCare brand was originally architected under a highly limiting, print-media framework. When applied to digital products, the assets felt rigid, lacked scalability, and restricted dynamic user interactions. With a shift to digital interactions during and after the pandemic, different digital product teams across the organization started creating their own set of assets to promote our loyalty programs in different places. The result was a mismatched set of banners, cards, language guides, icons and illustrations that felt inconsistent, dated, and did not communicate the brand well.</p>

      <h3>The Strategy</h3>
      <p>Seeing this as a problem that needed to be addressed, I volunteered to tackle it and scale a new system that could be used across different product teams and in different ecosystems. I led the initiative to adapt and modernize the print strategy for a digital-first medium. I reimagined the typography hierarchies, color usage, and spatial layouts to ensure accessibility, responsiveness, and visual impact across web and mobile platforms without losing core brand equity.</p>

      <h3>The Value</h3>
      <p>Successfully bridged the gap between traditional brand marketing and modern product design, giving our product teams a flexible, scalable visual language to build with.</p>

